From 312043159ace1b13a416b606308ffdb53e429c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Walker <59085866+jaso1000@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:55:20 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Incoming calls + two-way audio: conditional
 preconditions, caller ID, callee BYE, VoIP audio mode, RNNoise bypass + AGC

- Incoming 183/200: only Require/offer QoS preconditions if the caller offered them
  (Telstra CANCELs otherwise); send 180 Ringing after an early-media 183 is PRACKed
- One local To-tag per incoming dialog (was random per response -> 481 on our BYE)
- Callee-side BYE via commonHeaders (Via/Route/Security-Verify) to the INVITE Contact
- Caller ID: set EXTRA_OIR/EXTRA_CNAP (missing OIR = presentation unknown = hidden)
- Real P-Access-Network-Info in 183/180 (shared helper)
- MmTelFeature.setCallAudioHandler(AUDIO_HANDLER_ANDROID) when each call is created, so
  Telecom uses MODE_IN_COMMUNICATION instead of MODE_IN_CALL (Samsung HAL otherwise gives
  the mic to the modem voice path)
- Bypass RNNoise (48 kHz model fed 8 kHz audio -> outputs silence) and add a simple AGC
  (capture level on this path is ~-50 dBFS); per-second uplink diagnostics

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
